Z||000000||JayUSA77||08-05-2001||03:05 PM||||hey guys i just currently bought a alarm for my car and i need to hook up the negative trunk wire so i can unlock the trunk by using my alarm but i cant because i dont know where the negative trunk wire IS and What COLOR it is. So basically my question is where is it in the car and what is its color. I have no idea so any help would be appreciated.<BR>j<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||ka4nkf||08-05-2001||04:12 PM||||I don't think there is a negative wire in the trunk lid. the auto latch makes its ground thru the latch||||reg||1
Z||000002||JohnF||08-05-2001||04:19 PM||||"Negative" trunk wire?  Don't think so.  For all wiring diagrams, go here: <A HREF="http://home.t-online.de/home/u.moeller-objects/schaltp.html" TARGET=_blank>http://home.t-online.de/home/u.moeller-objects/schaltp.html</A> ||||reg||6
Z||000003||theogre||08-05-2001||04:29 PM||||Ka4 is correct. the latch is opened thru a switched hot lead.<P>To work properly with the remote, you'll need a second relay. The easiet place to connect it is next to the exisiting one.<P>You have to use the new relay to switch a 12V line to the trunk release wire. According to my drawings for an 87, this is the black and white wire on the OE relay. You have to verify this for your car. I have seen diferant colors of wire used in other years.<P>The best place to get power for the new relay is the orange and dark blue wire on the trunk release switch. This way the same fuse is used for the new part of the circuit. It will make future repairs much simpler.||||reg||1
